WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.109
Host: What does a positive no-template control
suggest?

2
00:00:04.109 --> 00:00:11.642
Guide: It suggests contamination or
nonspecific signal and requires investigation
before interpreting the samples.

3
00:00:11.642 --> 00:00:15.581
Guide: It is not evidence of a true target in
every specimen.

4
00:00:15.581 --> 00:00:19.515
Host: A PCR tube lacks one of the two primers.

5
00:00:19.515 --> 00:00:23.333
Host: What is the main consequence for the
intended target?

6
00:00:23.333 --> 00:00:28.347
Guide: Efficient exponential amplification of
the bounded target is lost.

7
00:00:28.347 --> 00:00:34.225
Guide: The two primers define opposite ends
and support amplification of both strands.
